    "narrative": "Our strongest plays today center on high-leverage speed and favorable matchups against mid-tier arms. **Tyler Freeman** (64.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.78) lead the charge; **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and an 11% SP skill edge against Singer, while **Geraldo Perdomo** leverages an optimal #2 hole assignment to maximize his opportunity to catalyze the lineup. **Masyn Winn** (61.81) is a mandatory start today as he faces Kelly, who carries a shaky 5.29 xERA, providing a 19% SP skill advantage that makes him a high-floor candidate for stolen bases. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (60.69) is primed for a productive outing, utilizing a 13% platoon edge against Cavalli in a favorable park environment.\n\nThe toughest decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Luis Arraez** (44.52) on the bench. While his batting average profile is typically a stabilizer, he faces a daunting matchup against Miller (2.85 xERA), whose elite skill level suppressed **Luis Arraez**\u2019s efficiency score below the 50-point threshold. We opted for the higher-ceiling outcomes provided by **Gavin Sheets** and **Dylan Beavers**, whose matchups against more hittable pitching provided better paths to R/RBI volume. Please note that **Cal Raleigh** remains a marginal play at 53.78; he is battling a difficult park factor and a restrictive platoon split, so keep an eye on his game flow as we monitor our daily innings/game caps. **Bryce Harper** is confirmed to be off the board today with a scheduled day off, removing our highest-ceiling threat from the active rotation.",
